Thinking: We need to answer using the skill. Explain missing tileSize:256, CORS, maybe attribution, minzoom/maxzoom optional. Also need to add source to map and layer. Provide full example. Also mention need to add raster layer with appropriate beforeId to not hide labels. Also mention glyphs/sprite not needed for raster. Provide troubleshooting steps.

Below is a quick “check‑list” for a **plain OSM raster tileset** (`https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png`).  
If you follow the steps in order the source will appear and it won’t accidentally hide the basemap’s labels.

| What you have | What you still need | Why it matters |
|---------------|--------------------|----------------|
| ```js\n{ type: 'raster', tiles: ['https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'] }\n``` | **`tileSize: 256`** | OSM tiles are 256 px. MapLibre’s raster default is 512 px, so without this the imagery is rendered at the wrong zoom level (you’ll see a “zoom‑off” map). |
|               | **`attribution` (optional but recommended)** | OSM’s licence requires you to show attribution. It won’t stop the tiles from drawing, but it’s good practice and some style‑inspectors warn if it’s missing. |
|               | **Add the source to the map (`map.addSource`)** | The JSON object alone does nothing until you register it. |
|               | **Add a raster layer that uses the source** | A source without a layer is invisible. |
|               | **Insert the raster layer *below* the first `symbol` layer** (or any label layer) | If you just `map.addLayer()` with no second argument the raster sits on top of everything and will cover street‑name labels. |
|               | **CORS headers on the tile server** | OSM already sends `Access‑Control‑Allow‑Origin: *`, so you’re fine here. |
|               | **`minzoom` / `maxzoom` (optional)** | OSM serves 0‑19. If you omit them MapLibre will assume `maxzoom: 22`, which just results in a few empty requests at the very highest zooms – not a breaking problem. |

---

## Minimal working example

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>OSM raster source in MapLibre</title>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.js"></script>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@4.4.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    body, html { margin:0; height:100%; }
    #map { width:100%; height:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>
<script>
  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: {
      version: 8,
      // a very bare‑bones style – just a background and the OSM raster we add later
      sources: {},
      layers: [
        { id: 'background', type: 'background', paint: { 'background-color': '#e0e0e0' } }
      ]
    },
    center: [0, 0],
    zoom: 2
  });

  map.on('load', () => {
    // 1️⃣ Register the raster source
    map.addSource('osm-raster', {
      type: 'raster',
      tiles: ['https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'],
      tileSize: 256,               // ← essential for correct zoom
      attribution: '&copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors',
      // optional but nice:
      // minzoom: 0,
      // maxzoom: 19
    });

    // 2️⃣ Find the first symbol layer (labels) in the default style.
    //    If you are using a custom style you may need to adjust the ID.
    const firstSymbolId = map.getStyle().layers.find(l => l.type === 'symbol')?.id;

    // 3️⃣ Add the raster layer *below* that symbol layer
    map.addLayer(
      {
        id: 'osm-raster-layer',
        type: 'raster',
        source: 'osm-raster',
        paint: {}
      },
      firstSymbolId   // ← second argument makes it insert before the labels
    );
  });
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

### What each line does

| Line | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| `type: 'raster'` | Tells MapLibre we are dealing with image tiles. |
| `tiles: [...]` | The URL template that resolves to PNG tiles. |
| `tileSize: 256` | **Required** for OSM’s 256 px tiles (otherwise the map looks “zoomed out”). |
| `attribution` | Legal requirement; also shows up in the map’s UI if you enable the default `attributionControl`. |
| `firstSymbolId` | Looks up the first `symbol` layer (usually a label layer) so we can insert our raster **under** it. |
| `map.addLayer(..., firstSymbolId)` | Places the raster layer just before the label layer, preserving street‑name visibility. |

---

## Quick diagnostic checklist (if you still see a blank map)

| Symptom | What to look at first |
|---------|-----------------------|
| **No network requests at all** | Open DevTools → Network → filter “tile”. If nothing appears, the source may not have been added or the map never reached `load`. |
| **Requests return 404** | Verify the URL template works directly in the browser (e.g., `https://tile.openstreetmap.org/2/1/1.png`). |
| **Requests succeed (200) but you see a gray/blank area** | Check `tileSize`. If it’s still the default 512 you’ll get a zoom‑offset. |
| **Tiles appear but labels are missing** | You probably added the raster layer **after** the label layers. Use the second argument of `addLayer` (or reorder the style JSON) to insert it below the first `symbol` layer. |
| **Tiles appear but are shifted or stretched** | Double‑check that the map’s `crs` is the default Web Mercator (`EPSG:3857`). OSM tiles are only available in that projection. |
| **CORS error in console** | OSM already sends `Access‑Control‑Allow‑Origin: *`. If you switch to a self‑hosted raster server, you’ll need to enable CORS on that server. |

---

### TL;DR – What you were missing

```js
{
  type: 'raster',
  tiles: ['https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png'],
  tileSize: 256,                     // <‑‑ essential
  attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap contributors' // optional but recommended
}
```

…and **add a raster layer that is inserted before the first `symbol` layer** so the OSM labels stay visible.

That’s all you need for a functional OSM raster basemap in MapLibre. Happy mapping!
